From 6373ae88b90efca96b1092bece15a15492a2911d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@st.com>
Date: Fri, 22 May 2026 13:27:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 503/572] fix(st-drivers): use BIT_32/GENMASK_32 in ST drivers

The ST peripherals registers are 32 bit, use explicit BIT_32/GENMASK_32
when reading from/writing to those registers. This avoids warnings when
the drivers are compiled for AARCH64 platforms (STM32MP2).
For example:
drivers/st/clk/clk-stm32-core.c:727:22: warning: implicit conversion
 loses integer precision: 'uint64_t' (aka 'unsigned long') to 'uint32_t'
 (aka 'unsigned int')
      [-Wshorten-64-to-32]
  727 |         uint32_t mask_rdy = BIT(gate->bit_idx);
      |                  ~~~~~~~~   ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git 43d4ae2740450e3aa03cee1e4827e3f29b3e9cc5 fix(st-drivers): use BIT_32/GENMASK_32 in ST drivers]
Change-Id: I2510111f8b3e3bc3382f2bc35691451393435427
Signed-off-by: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/tf-a/+/572143
Tested-by: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Maxime MERE <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
---
 drivers/st/clk/clk-stm32-core.c   | 44 +++++++++++++++----------------
 drivers/st/clk/clk-stm32-core.h   |  4 +--
 drivers/st/clk/clk-stm32mp2.c     | 18 ++++++-------
 drivers/st/crypto/stm32_rng.c     |  4 +--
 drivers/st/gpio/stm32_gpio.c      | 10 +++----
 drivers/st/reset/stm32mp2_reset.c |  4 +--
 drivers/st/rif/stm32_rifsc.c      |  4 +--
 7 files changed, 44 insertions(+), 44 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/st/clk/clk-stm32-core.c b/drivers/st/clk/clk-stm32-core.c
